    excerpt: 'Stop building 50-page reports. Learn how to define metrics and build real-time dashboards.',
    serviceSlug: 'data-analytics',
    category: 'Data Analytics',
    date: 'October 15, 2026',
    readTime: '6 min read',
    content: '<h2>The Problem with Traditional Reporting</h2><p>Most companies send out massive Excel reports every Monday. By Wednesday, the data is outdated, and nobody reads it. The solution is not a bigger report; it is a focused, real-time KPI dashboard.</p><h3>1. Define the Metric in Code</h3><p>What exactly is "Active User"? Is it someone who logged in? Or someone who made a purchase? We define these metrics in SQL and dbt models so the definition is consistent across the whole company.</p><h3>2. The ETL Pipeline</h3><p>We use tools like Apache Airflow to pull data from your CRM, Stripe, and database every hour. We clean it, aggregate it, and load it into a data warehouse (like Snowflake or PostgreSQL).</p><h3>3. The Dashboard</h3><p>We build dashboards using Metabase or PowerBI. The dashboard should answer 3 questions: "What happened?", "Why did it happen?", and "What should we do next?". It should have filters for date ranges, regions, and products.</p>'
